---
import '../../styles/decision.css';
---

<section id="decision" class="decision-section section-pad">
  <div class="container split-grid">
    <div class="section-copy">
      <p class="label muted">Parent pain section</p>
      <h2>A marksheet is not a career map.</h2>
      <p>
        Class 8 to 10 is when career confusion quietly becomes career pressure.
      </p>
      <p>
        Marks can show academic performance, but they do not fully reveal whether a child is suited for Science,
        Commerce, Humanities, Design, Technology, Business, Research or other career directions.
      </p>
      <p>Most wrong stream decisions happen because families depend on only one signal: marks.</p>
      <p>A better decision needs four signals working together.</p>
      <ul class="decision-list">
        <li><strong>Aptitude:</strong> What the child can naturally understand and solve</li>
        <li><strong>Personality:</strong> What environments and roles suit the child</li>
        <li><strong>Interests:</strong> What the child is repeatedly drawn towards</li>
        <li><strong>Study style:</strong> How the child learns, focuses and handles pressure</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <figure class="image-card image-card-small">
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/images/parent.webp" type="image/webp" />
        <img src="/images/parent.jpg" alt="Parent and child reviewing study choices together" loading="lazy" width="800" height="598" />
      </picture>
      <figcaption>Guidance before the pressure of stream selection peaks.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
